Falsifies `allocation_cache::verification::the_heap_layout_is_never_empty_or_smaller`.

The defect: `heap_layout` stops making an empty request one byte long, so a request with no class
and no size reaches the heap as an empty layout, which a heap may refuse.

Expected to fail: the harness's claim that `heap.size() >= 1`; Kani reports the assertion
reachable for an empty request aligned past the grid.

diff --git a/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs b/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
index d42a4df59..1a669afca 100644
--- a/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/allocation_cache/src/lib.rs
@@ -130,7 +130,7 @@ pub const fn heap_layout(layout: Layout) -> Layout {
         // it (`layout.size()` was valid and one is the least valid size).
         None => unsafe {
             Layout::from_size_align_unchecked(
-                if layout.size() == 0 { 1 } else { layout.size() },
+                layout.size(),
                 layout.align(),
             )
         },
